# Security headers for static hosts that read a `_headers` file
# (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify). This file is copied verbatim into `out/` by the
# static export. It is NOT active on hosts that ignore `_headers` (e.g. plain
# Apache/Hostinger, Nginx) - see docs/DEPLOYMENT-SECURITY.md for those.
#
# These are conservative, non-breaking headers for a client-only static SPA.
# No CSP is set by default because a static export ships hashed inline runtime
# chunks; add one per host only after verifying it does not break the app.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
